# Goal Description

Expand the "Experimental Design & Statistics" suite by implementing the 6 requested bioinformatics and biostatistics tools. This will provide users with a comprehensive set of calculators and visualizers for survival analysis, dose-response curves, outlier detection, statistical test selection, multiple testing correction, and drug synergy.

> [!WARNING]
> Implementing 6 complex mathematical tools simultaneously is a massive undertaking. To ensure mathematical accuracy and high-quality UI/UX for each tool, I strongly recommend executing this plan in **phases**, starting with the highest-impact tools (Kaplan-Meier and IC50).

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Execution Strategy:** Because tools like IC50 (non-linear 4PL regression) and Kaplan-Meier (Log-rank test) require complex math and custom charting, should we implement them in phases (e.g., Phase 1: Navigation + IC50 + Kaplan Meier) to ensure they are thoroughly tested before moving to the smaller calculators?

> [!NOTE]
> **Math Libraries:** For complex curve fitting (like 4PL for IC50), implementing Levenberg-Marquardt optimization in pure TypeScript from scratch is possible but complex. Are you okay with me writing custom TypeScript mathematical solvers for these, as we did for the Variance Minimization engine?

